  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The giraffe stands on four capsule legs attached to a cylinder body. A long cylinder neck connects the body to an oval head. All pieces start with a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring-gi"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Yarn and yarn amounts"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You need approx. 37 g total: yellow for the main body, brown for the patch markings. Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "colour-change-gi"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "colour change"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " when working patch spots directly into rounds, or embroider them on afterwards."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Head"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 5 cm by 7 cm oval head (15 rounds). Fit "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "safety-eyes-gi"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "safety eyes"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at round 7."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Neck"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 4 cm diameter by 10 cm cylinder (28 rounds). Leave both ends open. Stuff firmly so the neck stands upright."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 8 cm diameter by 11 cm cylinder (31 rounds). Stuff firmly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Legs (make 4)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 2.5 cm diameter by 8 cm capsule (20 rounds). Use brown for the hoof section at the bottom 2 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pin all legs to the body base before sewing to check the giraffe stands flat. Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ladder-stitch-gi"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "ladder stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to sew each leg. Attach neck to the top-front of the body, then head to the top of the neck. Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "dc2tog-gi"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "dc2tog"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to close any loose join gaps."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The amigurumi zebra uses the same cylinder body shape with a shorter neck and black and white stripe markings."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
